{"t": "2026-10-06T12:22:03", "stage": "A1", "verb": "ask", "args": ["Stage A1 section 1 defines concept reach as the share of a room's concepts that carry a theme_id. In this store every one of the 115388 concepts has a theme_id and sits in its theme's code_ids, so the share is 1.0 in all 705 rooms and no room size makes it fall. Did you mean another measure, for example concepts per second-order theme, or the share of concepts a theme's note or label actually describes? The threshold decides where cite.py must reach concepts at C2 to D3."], "opts": {"ids": "A1", "assume": "I declare concept_reach_threshold as 0 items: the measure gives no cut, and second-order themes grow at slope 0.23 on items against 0.53 for concepts, so every room is read at concept level from C2 to D3. I will revise it if your answer names another measure."}, "offset": 0, "limit": 80, "lines": 1, "total": 1, "refused": null}
